export const HELP_TEXT = "<!-- Generated by scripts/build-chat-help.js — edit js/chat-questions.js (or the rules in that script) instead. -->\n# KampongShare help\n\n## Site rules\n\n- KampongShare is a community donation and volunteer platform for Singapore. Local organizations post what they need; people donate items or volunteer at events.\n- Individual accounts can donate, volunteer, or both, on one account. Organization and admin accounts can't donate or volunteer. Nobody can sign up as an admin.\n- Signing up needs a name, email, password, agreeing to the Privacy Notice and confirming you are 18 or older. Phone, postal code and area are optional. We never ask for NRIC/FIN, date of birth, race, religion, income, health information or photos of people.\n- Donating: open Browse needs, press Offer on one item and choose how many (never more than is still needed). One active offer per item; to change the amount, cancel and offer again. The organization accepts or declines. Once accepted, the drop-off instructions show on the donor dashboard under \"Ready to drop off\". The organization marks it delivered; a request becomes fulfilled when everything is delivered.\n- When a request is closed, its waiting offers are declined automatically (\"Request closed\"); accepted offers still go ahead.\n- What can be donated: food, clothing, hygiene, household, baby and education items that organizations ask for. Food must be sealed, unopened and not past its expiry date. No cooked or home-made food and no medicines. Clothing should be clean and usable.\n- Volunteering: an admin approves new volunteer accounts first; until then you can only browse events. Then press Volunteer on an event; the organization approves each application. You can withdraw while it is waiting; once approved, contact the organization if you can't make it. When an event has all the volunteers it needs it shows \"Event full\".\n- Organizations: sign up as an organization, fill in the organization details, and wait for an admin to approve it. Then post requests (items, quantities, deadline, drop-off instructions) and events. An admin checks every request and event before the public sees it. After approval, a request's quantities, deadline, urgency and drop-off instructions can still change; its title, description and items can't. Closing a request can include a reason; cancelling an event needs a reason that volunteers will see. Requests still waiting for approval, and events nobody applied to, can be deleted.\n- Organizations see a donor's or volunteer's contact details only after that person makes an offer to them or applies to their event. The public never sees donors' or volunteers' names or contact details.\n- AI: each request gets an urgency score from a clear formula (deadline, how much is still needed, the organization's own urgency). The AI only explains the score and helps match what people can give. AI results are labelled \"AI-suggested\", the AI never receives personal details, and people always make the decisions.\n- History: past offers, applications, requests and events stay in a History tab for 12 months.\n- Accounts: sign up on the Sign up page (/signup.html); log in on the Log in page (/login.html) with email and password; log out from the Account menu at the top right. Forgot, reset or change a password: the site can't reset or change passwords yet (there is no reset link); email the address shown in the Privacy Notice (/privacy.html) and the team will help you get back in. The Profile page (/profile.html) lets you change your name, phone, postal code, area, donating/volunteering, availability, interests and skills (press Save changes), withdraw your consent, and see your data. Your email can't be changed on the site. People who donate or volunteer can delete their own account on the Profile page (\"Delete my account\", tick \"I understand this can't be undone\"): it removes the login, details and applications, cancels waiting offers, and keeps past donations without the name. Organization and admin accounts can't be deleted there: email the address shown in the Privacy Notice.\n- Pages: Browse needs (/needs.html), Sign up (/signup.html), Log in (/login.html), Profile (/profile.html), How it works (/#how-heading), Privacy Notice (/privacy.html).\n\n## Questions and answers\n\n### How do I donate?\n\nFind a request you can help with, then press Offer on one item and say how many you can give. The organization accepts or declines your offer. Once it's accepted, you'll see where and when to drop it off. You need a free account to offer, so organizations can arrange drop-off.\n\n### How do I volunteer?\n\nSign up and tick \"I want to volunteer\". An admin checks new volunteer accounts first. Once you're approved, open an event and press Volunteer. The organization then confirms your place. While you wait, you can still browse all the events.\n\n### How do offers work?\n\nAn offer is your promise to give a number of one item, never more than is still needed. You can have one active offer per item; to change the amount, cancel it and offer again. The organization accepts or declines it. If a request closes, waiting offers are declined automatically, but accepted ones still go ahead.\n\n### What can I donate?\n\nOnly what organizations ask for: food, clothing, hygiene, household, baby and education items. Food must be sealed, unopened and not past its expiry date — you'll tick a box to confirm this. Cooked or home-made food isn't accepted, and neither are medicines. Clothing should be clean and in good condition.\n\n### How does drop-off work?\n\nEach request has drop-off instructions from the organization, like an address and opening hours. Once your offer is accepted, they appear clearly on your dashboard under \"Ready to drop off\". Bring the items there, and the organization marks them delivered.\n\n### Can I donate and volunteer with one account?\n\nYes! One account can do both. Tick both when you sign up, or turn the other one on later in your profile. You'll then see a switch in the top bar to move between Donating and Volunteering. Turning on volunteering means an admin checks your volunteer account first.\n\n### How do I post a request?\n\nOnce an admin has approved your organization, go to Requests and press \"New donation request\". Add a title, the items and quantities you need, a deadline and drop-off instructions. An admin checks every request before donors can see it.\n\n### Why is my request waiting for approval?\n\nAn admin checks every new request before it goes public, to keep the platform safe and accurate. This usually doesn't take long. If it's rejected, you'll see the admin's note explaining what to change. While it's waiting, you can still edit or delete it.\n\n### How do I accept offers?\n\nOpen Offers. Each offer shows the item, the amount and the donor's contact details, so you can arrange drop-off. Press Accept or Reject. When the items arrive, press \"Mark delivered\". The request becomes fulfilled automatically once everything has been delivered.\n\n### How do I cancel an event?\n\nOpen Events and press \"Cancel event\". You'll need to give a short reason, because approved volunteers and anyone with the event's link will see it. If nobody has applied yet, you can delete the event instead.\n\n### How do I sign up?\n\nPress Sign up and choose whether you're an individual or an organization. Individuals tick \"I want to donate\", \"I want to volunteer\" or both. You'll need your name, email and a password, and you must agree to the Privacy Notice and confirm you're 18 or older. Phone, postal code and area are optional.\n\n### How do I log in or log out?\n\nTo log in, press Log in at the top and enter your email and password. To log out, open the Account menu at the top right and press Log out.\n\n### I forgot my password\n\nSorry — the site can't reset passwords yet, and there's no way to change your password on the site. Please email us using the address in the Privacy Notice, and we'll help you get back in.\n\n### How do I change my details?\n\nOpen your Profile. You can change your name, phone, postal code and area, turn donating or volunteering on or off, and update when you're free, your interests and skills. Then press Save changes. Your email can't be changed on the site yet.\n\n### How do I delete my account?\n\nIf you donate or volunteer: open your Profile, go to \"Delete my account\", tick \"I understand this can't be undone\" and confirm. This removes your login, details and applications; past donations stay with organizations without your name. Organization accounts can't be deleted there — please email us using the address in the Privacy Notice.\n\n### How does the AI work?\n\nEach request gets an urgency score from a clear formula: how close the deadline is, how much is still needed, and the organization's own urgency. The AI only explains the score in plain words and helps match what you can give. It never sees anyone's personal details. Everything it suggests is labelled \"AI-suggested\", and people always make the decisions.\n\n### Who checks the requests?\n\nOur admins. They approve every organization before it can post anything, and every request and event before the public can see it. If something looks wrong later, they can close it or cancel it.\n\n### How is my information protected?\n\nYou can read how we handle your information in our Privacy Notice.\n";

